# apps/www — institutional marketing site (www.zephyraconsultora.com).
#
# This app carries NO AUTH (domain-boundaries v1.1 §4), so none of the session /
# JWT / HMAC secrets belong here. Do not add SESSION_SECRET, LEARNER_JWT_SECRET
# or MAGIC_LINK_HMAC_KEY to this file — if a change appears to need one, the
# change belongs in apps/academia or apps/backoffice instead.

# Convex — the public content (blog, projects, team, clients, services) is read
# client-side through useQuery, and @zephyra/ui/providers/ConvexProvider builds a
# ConvexReactClient at MODULE scope. `next build` therefore needs this var to be
# a syntactically valid URL even though nothing is fetched at build time (every
# page is `export const dynamic = "force-dynamic"`).
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL=https://xxx.convex.cloud

# Contact form (/api/send-mail).
# PRIMARY: Resend. EMAIL_FROM must be on a domain verified in the Resend
# dashboard. FALLBACK (legacy Ferozo SMTP) is used only when RESEND_API_KEY is
# absent — that is why EMAIL_USER / EMAIL_PASSWORD are still listed.
RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxx
EMAIL_FROM=Zephyra <no-reply@zephyraconsultora.com>
EMAIL_USER=tu-cuenta-smtp@example.com
EMAIL_PASSWORD=tu-password-smtp

# App
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL was declared in this file but read by nothing in apps/www
# (verified at M4 by grep over apps/www/src), and it is retired platform-wide in
# favour of the per-app NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL.
#
# This section used to open "NO URL VARIABLE IS NEEDED HERE", and that is NO
# LONGER TRUE — see the three below. It also anticipated exactly this case: "if a
# flow here ever needs to link to academia or backoffice, add
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ACADEMIA_URL / NEXT_PUBLIC_BACKOFFICE_URL and read it through
# requireOrigin() from @zephyra/utils — never a hardcoded host." That is what the
# apex 301 map does.
#
# www remains the only app that generates no outbound URLs IN CONTENT: per
# boundaries v1.1 §5 its single email — the contact-form notification from
# /api/send-mail — is addressed to Zephyra's own inbox
# (info@zephyraconsultora.com) and carries no link back into any app. The
# variables below are consumed by next.config.ts at BUILD time, not by any page.
#
# www is served from the APEX zephyraconsultora.com; www.* 301s to the apex
# (boundaries v1.1 §3.1, ruled 2026-07-28, revocable on registrar evidence).

# The two apps the apex redirects to, and this app's own origin.
#
# REQUIRED — `next build` fails without the first two. next.config.ts feeds all
# three to src/lib/cutover-redirects.ts, which builds the 301 map from the apex to
# the routes that moved off it (/cursos/*, /empresa/*, /admin/*, and the three
# auth paths /login, /forgot-password, /reset-password).
#
# WHY IT THROWS INSTEAD OF SKIPPING THE REDIRECTS. An empty redirect list is
# indistinguishable from a working one until a real visitor hits an old URL — and
# the first people to hit one are Zephyra's own staff at /login, an invited
# learner at /empresa/invitacion, and a buyer returning from MercadoPago. None of
# those show up by clicking around the new site.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL is this app's own origin and is used ONLY as a loop guard:
# if either destination below resolves to it, the apex would redirect these paths
# to itself until the browser aborts, so the build refuses. It is optional — the
# guard is skipped when absent — but set it, because three projects with three
# sets of similar hostnames is a very easy place to paste the wrong value.
#
# Production: academia.zephyraconsultora.com / backoffice.zephyraconsultora.com /
# zephyraconsultora.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_ACADEMIA_URL=http://localhost:3000
NEXT_PUBLIC_BACKOFFICE_URL=http://localhost:3002
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3001
